---
/**
 * The idea behind the studio, stated plainly. Leads with the outcome (clarity,
 * momentum); the tooling never opens. The "signal over noise" motif carries
 * the section.
 */
---

<section class="s-section s-manifesto">
  <p class="s-label" data-s-fade>01 · The idea</p>

  <h2 class="s-statement s-display" data-s-lines>
    <span class="s-mask"><span class="s-mask-inner">Signal over</span></span>
    <span class="s-mask"><span class="s-mask-inner">noise, always.</span></span>
  </h2>

  <div class="s-manifesto-cols">
    <p data-s-fade>
      Most software is built on guesses and ships late. We start from the one
      thing that matters: the outcome you are trying to move, agreed in plain
      language before a line is written.
    </p>
    <p data-s-fade>
      From there it is fast and deliberate. Clear scope, working increments you
      can see, and a product that earns its place. Built to hold up long after
      launch day.
    </p>
  </div>

  <span class="s-rule" data-s-rule aria-hidden="true"></span>
</section>

<style>
  .s-manifesto-cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 4rem);
    max-width: 920px;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.6rem, 7vh, 4rem);
  }
  .s-manifesto-cols p {
    max-width: 44ch;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.3vw, 1.12rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--s-muted);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .s-manifesto-cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
